/-!
# `G(ℤ)` and `H(ℤ)` with rational breakpoints consist of their generators

Monod (p. 2) takes `G(ℤ)` with rational breakpoints to be the *set* of piecewise `PSL(2, ℤ)`
homeomorphisms of `P¹` with breakpoints in `ℚ ∪ {∞}`; the bundle defines `GRat` as the subgroup
generated by that set. They agree: the set is already a subgroup. The only non-formal point is
that such a map sends `ℚ ∪ {∞}` into itself, also at a breakpoint `b`, where it agrees with a
single Möbius map on one side of `b` and hence, by continuity, at `b` itself.

The Möbius-map and one-sided-germ helpers are taken from the Monod mission's proof of
`Monod.mem_G_iff_isPiecewiseProj`.
-/

